    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1209">

                <pb facs="0984" n="868" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg868"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/5494.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Acapulco to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Acapulco</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-14T15:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 14, 1912—3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Rebel leader Padilla controls all coast region to north of Acapulco. All
                    Government troops have retreated to Acapulco.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry K. Pangburn.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
